[font=Palatino Linotype][center][size=6][b][color=#6FCB9F]Bureau of Private Dispatches[/color][/b][/size]
[color=#8C8A82]Never lose an incoming whisper in a busy chat.[/color][/center]



[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 1.1.012551[/color]

Compact UI update and safer reply tracking.

- Fixed outgoing reply resolution: an explicit recipient is no longer replaced by the current chat target, preventing another sender's unanswered notification from being marked answered and lost.
- Hover tooltips now show the full cleaned latest message above the available actions. Restored cards without message text keep their explanatory placeholder.
- Removed letter identity seals and inline group, friend, and guild glyphs. Sender-colored rails remain; relation details stay in the tooltip.
- Compact rows now use separate areas for the sender name and muted message preview, with stable unread, status, time, and dismiss positions.
- Replaced header symbols with stock ESO lock, collapse, and clear-all icons. Header title and count areas are bounded to avoid overlapping controls.
- Six notifications are visible by default. A new setting selects 6, 8, or 12 per page without reloading or discarding tracked senders; the choice is saved account-wide.
- Softened hover highlights and arrival/reminder pulses, made counters more neutral, and kept existing font sizes.
- Updated English and Russian settings text and documentation for the new layout.



[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 1.0.131353[/color]

First public release.

- One notification per sender account `@id`, with unread count, relative time, and a sender-colored identity seal.
- Adaptive stack: the newest or currently reminded sender is expanded, older senders use compact rows, and extra senders page through overflow.
- Rows stay put under the pointer. Incoming whispers never jump the card you are looking at or dragging.
- Left-click opens a reply without clearing the card. The cycle closes only after an observed outgoing whisper, or after an explicit hide.
- Read, answered, and dismissed are separate. Mark read clears unread; hide moves the sender onto a session-only undo tape; answering confirms the cycle.
- Follow-up timers: waiting, one overdue reminder, reply-composer grace, and a brief answered card. Reminders wait through combat, menus, and interaction.
- Incoming sound, mute, five-minute DND, and auto-DND in combat. Cards still collect while alerts are held.
- Unanswered whispers survive `/reloadui` without storing message text. If pChat is loaded, its in-memory history may fill the restored preview.
- Card gestures in the hover tooltip: reply, open chat, mark read, hide, mail, teleport, and ignore (Ctrl+Alt+Right with a confirmation dialog).
- Relation glyph with a fixed priority: group, friend, then guild.
- Keyboard bindings in Controls: reply, next/previous, mark read, collapse, clear, mute, DND, restore, and lock. Reply does not overwrite typed chat.
- Movable account-wide panel with lock, scale, background opacity, combat auto-collapse, and screen clamping.
- Settings panel via LibAddonMenu-2.0. `/bpd settings` and `/bpdsettings` open it. English and Russian localization.

[/font]
